d native OS.","url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/aienos/pull/2","pr":2},{"id":"chip","repo":"omega","date":"2026-09-26","title":"First Omega GB10 vector-add evidence","status":"Chip evidence","detail":"Native GB10 vector addition is reported on physical silicon. Qualification applies to the specific operation and candidate, not to the entire computing stack.","url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/omega/pull/22","pr":22},{"id":"repair","repo":"omega","date":"2026-09-30","title":"Resident accelerator foundation repaired","status":"Chip evidence","detail":"M19R corrective qualification records the combined foundation admission result. Evidence identity and runtime lifecycle are tightened before building higher layers.","url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/omega/pull/111","pr":111},{"id":"compiler","repo":"omega","date":"2026-10-01","title":"A compiler, contracts and ownership","status":"Host evidence","detail":"OSC-1 adds source to typed IR to AArch64. October 1 follow-ups add executable contracts, structs, arenas and generation-safe handles. This is a compiler slice with host evidence; it is not self-hosting.","url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/omega/pull/144","pr":144},{"id":"ck","repo":"aienos","date":"2026-10-01","title":"Native C kernel boots in QEMU","status":"QEMU evidence","detail":"The C kernel core enters the UEFI boot path. Follow-ups attach storage, capability authority, SMMU services and artifact loading. Physical C-kernel qualification remains unestablished.","url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/aienos/pull/194","pr":194},{"id":"r16","repo":"omega","date":"2026-10-01","title":"Requalification exposes real blockers","status":"Fail evidence","detail":"On a pinned silicon candidate, R12 to R14 pass, R15 fails two gates with an Xid 109 timeout, and R16 fails inventory gates. This preserves failure as project progress in evidence quality.","url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/omega/pull/171","pr":171},{"id":"tensor","repo":"omega","date":"2026-10-01","title":"Tensor semantics reach main","status":"Host evidence","detail":"Immutable tensors, views, broadcasting, reductions and matmul merge with CPU evidence. GB10 realization and reverse-mode autodiff are in separate open PRs; those implementations are not included in the measured default-branch code totals.","url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/omega/pull/136","pr":136},{"id":"fence","repo":"aienos","date":"2026-10-01","title":"Virtio DMA confinement demonstrated","status":"QEMU evidence","detail":"VIRTIO_F_ACCESS_PLATFORM plus an out-of-window DMA test prove confinement in QEMU. Hardware remains NOT_RUN.","url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/aienos/pull/214","pr":214},{"id":"deadline","repo":"omega","date":"2026-10-01","title":"World deadlines become enforceable","status":"Host evidence","detail":"A returned reaction that overruns its logical deadline is cancelled before publish, with mutations discarded and its resource charge refunded. It cannot interrupt a reaction that never returns.","url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/omega/pull/183","pr":183}],"activity":[{"repo":"aienos","title":"native/kernel: C continuity codec, cut 1 of #222 [host PASS, QEMU n/a, hardware NOT_RUN]","number":227,"url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/aienos/pull/227","state":"Merged","date":"2026-10-01","timestamp":"2026-10-01T19:31:49Z"},{"repo":"omega","title":"HD-09: enforce declared deadline at publish (cancel on overrun)","number":183,"url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/omega/pull/183","state":"Merged","date":"2026-10-01","timestamp":"2026-10-01T19:25:54Z"},{"repo":"aien-protocols","title":"S1: TRN1 0.2.0 (types 17-21, 32-byte cause id) [NOT_RUN]","number":12,"url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/aien-protocols/pull/12","state":"Merged","date":"2026-10-01","timestamp":"2026-10-01T19:23:10Z"},{"repo":"aien-architecture","title":"HD-08: TRN1 0.2.0 spec amendments (Q2-Q5, Q7, type 20, schema 3)","number":102,"url":"https://github.com/aien-dev/aien-architecture/pull/102","state":"Merged","date":"2026-10-01","timest